owing the text above)) [LOW CONFIDENCE: 0.00 / UNRELIABLE — Rely strictly on surrounding written SOP text and do not guess unverified parameters]:\nVLM Analysis FAILED (non-retryable error): [503] {'message': 'ResourceExhausted: Worker local total request limit reached (16/16)', 'type': 'Service Unavailable', 'code': 503}\n{'error': {'message': 'ResourceExhausted: Worker local total request limit reached (16/16)', 'type': 'Service Unavailable', 'code': 503}, 'status': 503}\n\nStep 3: Caller identity verified\nNavigation: CoreID Admin Console → user profile → Identity Verification panel\nAsk the caller for at least 2 of: employee ID, manager's name, department, or last 4 digits of the phone on file. ✅ Do not send a one-time code to the user — your own admin session already satisfies the authentication requirement; this checklist is what verifies the caller is who they claim to be. If fewer than 2 items match, stop and escalate to your team lead rather than proceeding.\n\n### Visual Inspection Report (Image 3 (inline, following the text above)) [HIGH CONFIDENCE: 0.98 — Fully trust and extract visible UI buttons, IDs, and parameters]:\nSCREEN / CONTEXT: CoreID Admin Console > J. Employee — Identity Verification  \nUI ACTION: Verify identity by confirming “Employee ID matches ticket” and “Manager name matches ticket” are checked  \nVISIBLE ENTITIES: Employee ID matches ticket (checked); Manager name matches ticket (checked); Department matches record (unchecked); Last 4 digits of phone on file (unchecked); 2 of 4 confirmed — minimum required to proceed; Signed in as A. Rao (L1 Support — Password Reset Admin)  \nERRORS: None visible  \nCONFIDENCE SCORE: 0.98  \nCONFIDENCE LEVEL: High  \nCONFIDENCE REASON: UI is clear, legible, and checkbox states are distinctly visible.\n\nStep 4: Temporary password issued\nNavigation: CoreID Admin Console → user profile → Reset Password\nSelect Generate Temporary Password. Leave Force change at next sign-in checked — this is the default